<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Thorpe returns two weeks after V-excision of the lower lip cancer by Dr. Ferrante. The CT of the neck before surgery showed no enlarged or abnormal lymph nodes. He took acetaminophen for three days after the operation and needed nothing stronger. The stitches were removed last week. His lip feels a little tight but he can whistle, drink from a cup and speak clearly. He has had no chest tightness since the first week of his medicines and has not used nitroglycerin. He took aspirin throughout and had only slight oozing on the first night. He is keen to start cardiac rehabilitation. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Surgery</td><td>V-excision two weeks ago; stitches out; lip function normal</td></tr><tr><td>Neck CT before surgery</td><td>No enlarged or abnormal lymph nodes</td></tr><tr><td>Angina</td><td>None for four weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Aspirin, atorvastatin 80 mg and metoprolol taken daily</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

