    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Squamous cell carcinoma of the left lower lip, excised (C00.1)</content>. Pathology: invasive keratinizing squamous cell carcinoma, well differentiated, 1.3 cm, depth of invasion 2.5 mm, no perineural or lymphovascular invasion, all margins clear (closest, deep, 6 mm). With a clinically and radiologically negative neck, this is pathologic T1, clinical N0, stage I. No further treatment is needed; the neck is observed because the depth of invasion is small. Surveillance follows the NCCN schedule. [S]<list><item>Lip, mouth and neck examination every 1 to 3 months for the first year.</item><item>Lip balm with sunscreen and a hat; skin checks.</item><item>Dental check-up.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic coronary disease with stable angina (I25.119)</content>. No angina for four weeks; blood pressure 128/78. LDL 68 mg/dL from 158, a 57% fall on atorvastatin 80 mg, but above the secondary-prevention goal of 55 mg/dL. ALT 31 U/L; no muscle symptoms. [S]<list><item>Add ezetimibe 10 mg daily.</item><item>Lipid panel in 8 to 10 weeks.</item><item>Begin cardiac rehabilitation, three sessions a week.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Examination of the lips, mouth, and neck</td><td>Every 1 to 3 months in year 1, 2 to 6 months in year 2, 4 to 8 months in years 3 to 5, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Scar healing; no nodularity; no neck nodes</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Pathology: type, margins, depth of invasion, perineural and lymphovascular invasion</td><td>Full pathology after excision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>pT1, depth of invasion 2.5 mm, margins clear (closest 6 mm), no perineural or lymphovascular invasion</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Imaging of the primary site and neck</td><td>Before treatment as indicated; afterwards only for symptoms or findings</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Neck CT before surgery: no abnormal nodes; no routine imaging afterwards</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>TSH</td><td>Every 6 to 12 months only if the neck was irradiated</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Neck not irradiated</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sun protection of the lips and skin</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Using lip balm with sunscreen and a hat</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Tobacco and alcohol use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tobacco-free; alcohol one or two beers some weekends</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Dental evaluation</td><td>After diagnosis, then routine</td><td>Due</td><td>Dental check-up advised; he will look into options</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure (goal below 130/80)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>128/78</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight, BMI, and physical activity</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>93.0 kg, BMI 27.2</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Angina frequency and nitroglycerin use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None for four weeks; no nitroglycerin</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and side effects: aspirin, high-intensity statin, beta-blocker</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>All taken daily; no muscle symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipid panel</td><td>4 to 12 weeks after starting or changing lipid therapy, then every 3 to 12 months; goal LDL below 55 mg/dL</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Five weeks after starting atorvastatin: total cholesterol 136, LDL 68, HDL 42, triglycerides 130 mg/dL; ezetimibe added</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>ALT on statin</td><td>Baseline; repeat only for symptoms</td><td>Completed today</td><td>31 U/L</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Cardiac rehabilitation</td><td>After a heart attack or for stable angina: up to 36 sessions</td><td>Referred</td><td>Starting this month, three sessions a week</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Lip cancer removed with clear margins and no recurrence on surveillance through four months. In progress; target 2026-10-26 [S]</item><item>LDL cholesterol below 55 mg/dL on secondary prevention. In progress; target 2026-09-21 [S]</item><item>Blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg. In progress; target 2026-09-21 [S]</item><item>Complete cardiac rehabilitation and walk uphill without angina. In progress; target 2026-10-26 [S]</item><item>Stay tobacco-free and protect his lips and skin from the sun. In progress; target 2026-10-26 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Head and Neck Cancers (cancer of the lip and oral cavity) (2026); 2023 AHA/ACC/ACCP/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline for the Management of Patients With Chronic Coronary Disease (2023); 2018 AHA/ACC/AACVPR/AAPA/ABC/ACPM/ADA/AGS/APhA/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline on the Management of Blood Cholesterol (2018); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, ischemic heart disease monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Cardiac rehabilitation three times a week. Visit in about ten weeks with a lipid panel and lip examination. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-21: coronary disease review in cardiac rehabilitation, lipid recheck after ezetimibe, and lip surveillance. [S]</paragraph></text>

